research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-92-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-93-> [L1] Continuity at $x$ is equivalent to $\omega_f(x)=0$, and each set $\{x:\omega_f(x)\ge\varepsilon\}$ is closed for $\varepsilon>0$ (`def-oscillation-in-rn`, `lem-oscillation-characterisation-in-rn`). Since every positive real is larger than $1/r$ for some natural $r\ge1$ (`cor-archimedean-reciprocal`), the discontinuity set is $\bigcup_{r\ge1}\{x:\omega_f(x)\ge1/r\}$.
