research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-8030-5.1 The Darboux gap is therefore below $\alpha\operatorname{vol}Q+2B\,\varepsilon/(4(B+1))<\varepsilon$. By [L3], $f$ is integrable.  [step 1.2, step 2.1, step 4.1, L3, algebra]
