research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-8032-6.1 By [L1], $D=\bigcup_{r\ge1}S_{1/r}$. Countable-union closure makes $D$ null, with countable choice used exactly through [[lem-null-sets-in-rn-closed-under-subsets-and-countable-unions]] and [[def-countable-choice]]. Together with step 5.1, this proves both directions using cover-nullity only.  [step 5.1, step 3.2, L1] ∎
