research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27584-+{"id":"lem-abel-transform-of-cesaro-means","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Ces%C3%A0ro_summation_methods","https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math322.pdf"],"rationale":"The literature records the generating-function relation behind Cesàro and Abel methods. The item isolates the exact zero-indexed transform with weights (n+1)(1-x)^2 and proves the algebra and convergence locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27585-+{"id":"thm-frobenius-cesaro-implies-abel-summability","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Ces%C3%A0ro_summation_methods","https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math322.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state that Cesàro (C,1) summability implies Abel summability to the same value. The item gives the zero-indexed weighted-kernel formulation and adapts the classical proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27586-+{"id":"cor-convergent-series-are-cesaro-and-abel-summable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Ces%C3%A0ro_summation_methods","https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-100c-real-analysis-fall-2012/1058808e5cb57c986118333f8b6fa0d7_MIT18_100CF12_l11sum.pdf","https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math322.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state regularity of Cesàro and Abel summation: ordinary convergence is preserved with the same sum. The item packages both consequences in the library's definitions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27587-+{"id":"lem-tauber-block-estimate","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Tauberian_theorems"],"rationale":"The source states Tauber's condition a_n=o(1/n) and its convergence consequence. The displayed block and weighted estimates are a bespoke elementary lemma extracted for the local proof, with a locally generated derivation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27588-+{"id":"thm-tauber-converse-for-abel-summability","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Tauberian_theorems"],"rationale":"The source states Tauber's converse: Abel summability plus a_n=o(1/n) implies ordinary convergence to the Abel sum. The item uses the equivalent shifted condition (n+1)a_n→0 and adapts the standard x_N=1-1/(N+1) proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27589-+{"id":"fs-power-series-uniform-on-its-open-interval","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Power_series"],"rationale":"The source states uniform convergence on compact subsets rather than on the whole open interval. The item formulates the stronger false claim and refutes it with the geometric series by an explicit local computation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27590-+{"id":"fs-power-series-convergence-at-one-point-forces-global-convergence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Power_series"],"rationale":"The source states radial convergence only inside the distance of a known convergence point and permits divergence farther out. The item turns the overstatement into a false statement and gives the geometric-series counterexample locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave13-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-27591-+{"id":"fs-abel-summability-implies-ordinary-convergence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math322.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Tauberian_theorems"],"rationale":"The sources explain that Abel summability alone need not imply ordinary convergence and use divergent Abel-summable examples. The item formulates the false converse and refutes it with Grandi's series.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
