research/audit/wave13-A3.md-53-  `sum k!(z-a)^k` as a radius-zero power series.
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-54-- The Rice notes state that for `|z|=1`, `z != 1`, the series `sum z^j` has
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-55-  Abel sum `(1-z)^(-1)`; `z=-1` is exactly the Grandi specialization with Abel
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-56-  value `1/2`, while ordinary divergence follows from its non-null terms.
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-57-- Lebl Proposition 10.5.1 states exactly that a bounded subset of `R^n` is
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-58-  Jordan measurable iff its ambient boundary is null.
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-59-- Lebl Example 10.1.9 states that a constant function on a rectangle integrates
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-60-  to the constant times the rectangle's volume; the unit-box item is its direct
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-61-  specialization.
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-62-- Munkres Section 14 defines a bounded set as rectifiable when its indicator is
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-63-  integrable, gives the null-boundary equivalence, and explicitly explains the
research/audit/wave13-A3.md-64-  borrowing of “rectifiable” from curve-length terminology.
