research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-62-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-63-### 1. `thm-jordan-boundary-criterion` — class (a), unambiguous falsehood and proof failure
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-64-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-65-Current Fact `[L1]` says:
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-66-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-67-> The indicator $1_E$ is discontinuous exactly at $\partial E$ (`def-metric-interior-closure-boundary`).
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-68-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-69-In this proof the indicator supplied by `thm-jordan-content-and-indicator-integrability` is a function on a bounding rectangle $Q$, not the global function on $\mathbb R^m$. The displayed equality is false for that relative-domain indicator. Take $E=Q=[0,1]^m$: then $1_E:Q\to\mathbb R$ is the constant function $1$ and has no discontinuities, while the ambient boundary $\partial E$ is nonempty. The literature proof states the equality for the global characteristic function on $\mathbb R^m$, not for an arbitrary restriction to $Q$: [Lebl, Jordan measurable sets](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_jordansets.html).
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-70-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-71-Consequently proof step 1.1 is not licensed by `[L1]` and `[L2]`, even though the theorem statement itself is standard and true. The smallest repair is to choose a rectangle whose interior contains the closure of $E$, which metric boundedness supplies by enlarging the rectangle already constructed in `[L3]`.
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-72-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-73-Proposed `[L1]`:
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-74-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-75-> [L1] If $Q$ is a nondegenerate rectangle with $\overline E\subseteq\operatorname{int}Q$, then the relative-domain indicator $1_E:Q\to\mathbb R$ is discontinuous exactly at the ambient boundary $\partial E$. At a boundary point every sufficiently small ball lies in $Q$ and meets both $E$ and its complement, while away from the boundary the indicator is locally constant (`def-metric-interior-closure-boundary`).
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-76-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-77-Proposed step 1.1:
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-78-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-79-> 1.1 By `[L3]`, choose a closed bounding rectangle $Q_0$ for $E$ and enlarge every coordinate interval by a fixed positive margin to obtain a nondegenerate rectangle $Q$ with $\overline E\subseteq Q_0\subseteq\operatorname{int}Q$. By `[L1]` and `[L2]`, $E$ is Jordan measurable exactly when $\partial E$ is null. `[L1, L2, L3, given]`
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-80-
research/audit/wave13-real-analysis.findings.md-81-Steps 1.2 and 2.1 may remain unchanged. This is a material repair: the stale `verification.judge` and `audited` state must be removed at A4, and the contract source/use entries must be regenerated from the repaired item.
